No iostreams (docs/gpu3d.md G1). Kosmos's libc++ is built without
localisation, so it has no std::ostream and no string streams. LLVM's
own coding standard keeps iostreams out of its libraries, and these are
the places that kept a string stream anyway: each becomes LLVM's own
raw_string_ostream, writing the same text - a hexadecimal number by
format_hex_no_prefix or utohexstr, a double as an ostream writes one, by
%g - and the files that reached <cctype> only through <sstream> include
it themselves. raw_os_ostream, which adapts to a std::ostream, is left
out where there is none.

